In-scope findings, for the doc-writer / test-writer:
MUST-FIX 1. Environment.pm:987 async filter example `my ( $value, @args, $cb ) = @_` -- @args swallows the callback, so $cb is always undef (tried it). Use `my $cb = pop; my ( $value, @args ) = @_;`.
SHOULD-FIX 2. Environment.pm:1100 says the callback "may be given in place of any of the optional arguments". Wrong: in the ignore_missing slot it counts as ignore_missing and is never called (get_template returns a no-op Template for a missing name). It replaces eager_compile or parent_name only, or goes 5th.
3. Environment.pm:1126 "With a callback it never dies": a non-string name dies before the callback (`render(undef, {}, $cb)`), as upstream. :1129 "a render without a callback that does defer fails": it returns undef silently, as upstream returns null (k104). :1130 with dev, a template-not-found error is still a Lib::Error.
4. Environment.pm:1222 Template compile "dies with the prettified Lib::Error": it dies with the raw TemplateError (`unexpected token: %}`, no path or line prefix), as upstream compile() does. TemplateError.pm:90 "already prefixed by update" is not true of that error, nor of the one get_exported passes to its callback (upstream getExported does cb(e) raw too, so the doc-writer's flag is no bug).
5. TemplateError.pm:104/:110 "counting from 1": render-time errors carry 0-based lineno/colno, as upstream (`a\nb {{ foo() }}` gives lineno 1, message [Line 1, Column 8]). Only parser and throwOnUndefined errors are 1-based (k106).
6. Environment.pm:1164 `load` fires "each time a loader's get_source returns a source": only when the loader emits it. FileSystem does; Precompiled does not, upstream neither.
7. Environment.pm:993 kwargs "a trailing Runtime keyword-arguments hash": name the class Text::Nunjucks::Runtime::KwArgs; for an async filter it comes before the callback. Nunjucks.pm:56 points users at Runtime's None but does not say how to reach it (Text::Nunjucks::Runtime->None), while Runtime.pm:1884 calls the whole module not an interface for applications. Carve None and KwArgs out there.
8. Nunjucks.pm:48 "the difference is a recorded decision, not an accident" is false today: there are open fidelity bugs (k49, k52, k53, k64, k74, k99, k103). Make it a policy sentence ("a deliberate difference is a recorded decision; any other difference is a bug"), or drop it until k24.
9. Precompiled.pm:71 "not part of the distribution yet" is roadmap wording for k23. Drop "yet" or the sentence.
10. t/00-synopsis.t does not check the "This prints" block (Nunjucks.pm:29). Changing it to `- B<C` in a scratch build still passed 10/10. Compare that block with the output too. :89 `>/dev/null` -> File::Spec->devnull.
